WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.785
- Hi my name's Nick and I know the first

00:00:01.785 --> 00:00:04.166
two words of the Canadian Nation Anthem.

00:00:05.966 --> 00:00:08.519
Americans Try to Sing "O Canada"

00:00:08.922 --> 00:00:11.139
- I'm excited to sing the
Canadian National Anthem.

00:00:11.139 --> 00:00:12.931
I know a *beep* about it.

00:00:12.931 --> 00:00:14.305
- My grandma's from Thunder Bay, Ontario

00:00:14.305 --> 00:00:15.771
and she sings it all the time.

00:00:15.771 --> 00:00:17.968
So I feel like I know the very beginning

00:00:17.968 --> 00:00:19.600
really, really well and then...

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:21.397
- I'm pretty sure I know all the words

00:00:21.397 --> 00:00:24.068
because I learned the song in Junior High

00:00:24.068 --> 00:00:25.728
because I was that kid.

00:00:25.728 --> 00:00:27.895
- But I've sung the
Canadian National Anthem

00:00:27.895 --> 00:00:29.438
plenty of times.

00:00:29.438 --> 00:00:32.520
- I lived in Canada for
four years. I'm American.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.611
I'm pretty sure I never learned O Canada.

00:00:35.611 --> 00:00:40.611
- ♫ O CANADA ♫

00:00:41.857 --> 00:00:46.681
- ♫ OUR HOME AND NATIVE LAND! ♫

00:00:47.161 --> 00:00:51.601
♫ TRUE PATRIOT LOVE ♫

00:00:51.877 --> 00:00:56.800
♫ IN ALL THY SONS COMMAND ♫

00:00:57.046 --> 00:01:00.157
- True patriot love in
all thy sons command.

00:01:00.587 --> 00:01:03.315
I don't think you should
command anyone to love you.

00:01:03.315 --> 00:01:05.179
- Sons and daughters...

00:01:05.409 --> 00:01:10.409
- ♫ WITH GLOWING HEARTS
WE SEE THEE RISE, ♫

00:01:10.491 --> 00:01:12.490
- I never really got why
your hearts would glow.

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:15.191
That seems like an E.T. related issue.

00:01:15.191 --> 00:01:20.023
♫ THE TRUE NORTH STRONG AND FREE ♫

00:01:20.023 --> 00:01:23.170
I love that they delineate
themselves as the true north.

00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:24.861
It's like North American sure,

00:01:24.861 --> 00:01:28.510
but the northern part, Canada,
that's worth celebrating.

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:30.506
- It sounds like Game of Thrones.

00:01:30.506 --> 00:01:35.506
- ♫ FROM FAR AND WIDE, O CANADA,
WE STAND ON GUARD FOR THEE♫

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:44.516
- I knew it was something like
far and wide and about the...

00:01:44.516 --> 00:01:46.108
I thought there was
something about the plains,

00:01:46.108 --> 00:01:47.776
but I couldn't even understand them.

00:01:47.776 --> 00:01:49.615
- They mean that because Canada only lives

00:01:49.615 --> 00:01:51.401
on the far and the wide.

00:01:51.401 --> 00:01:53.194
There's nothing in the center.

00:01:53.194 --> 00:01:58.194
♫ GOD KEEP OUR LAND ♫

00:01:59.174 --> 00:02:03.993
♫ GLORIOUS AND FREE! ♫

00:02:03.993 --> 00:02:08.993
♫ O CANADA, WE STAND ON GUARD FOR THEE. ♫

00:02:15.257 --> 00:02:20.257
♫ O CANADA, WE STAND ON GUARD FOR THEE. ♫

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:30.235
Play hockey!

00:02:30.235 --> 00:02:32.871
- I think you guys might
actually have it wrong.

00:02:32.932 --> 00:02:35.284
- Really the Canadian Nation
Anthem is blame Canada.

00:02:35.284 --> 00:02:38.928
Like come on, Salsbury wrote
it and that's what it is now.

00:02:39.251 --> 00:02:40.291
- Maple syrup, I don't know.

00:02:40.367 --> 00:02:42.407
- Oh my God! I knew none of these.

00:02:42.407 --> 00:02:43.577
- I think I nailed it.

00:02:43.577 --> 00:02:45.870
- Designed from like Christmas carol?

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:47.421
- I'm really in so much trouble.

00:02:47.421 --> 00:02:49.466
